  "instrument": "D-9 post-cutover verification: DNS/TLS/edge probe (verify.mjs) plus the canonical endpoint sweep (sweep2.mjs), both executed from GCP Cloud Build",
  "ranAt": "2026-09-17T20:35:12.153Z",
  "vantagePoint": "GCP Cloud Build (project smartcity-os-prod), deliberately not the fleet host. Two local instruments had to be excluded or they would have produced a false pass: (1) this host's resolver, which served a stale Google AAAA after the zone was already clean; (2) an AVG antivirus TLS-scanning proxy that re-signs every leaf certificate, so a local handshake reports the AVG issuer and cannot tell DigitalOcean's certificate from Google's.",
  "theQuestionThisAnswers": "After the GoDaddy records changed, when a client asks for smartcityos.io, which origin answers and with whose certificate? /api/health is byte-identical on both origins, so the body cannot distinguish them; the edge headers and the real certificate chain can.",
  "howOriginWasDistinguished": "App Platform's ingress is Cloudflare-fronted and returns server: cloudflare with a cf-ray header, and streams responses chunked. The Cloud Run original returns server: Google Frontend with an explicit Content-Length. Both were measured in the same run, so this is a direct comparison and not an inference.",
  "dnsGroundTruth": {
    "readFrom": "the GoDaddy authoritative nameservers (ns55/ns56.domaincontrol.com), then a public resolver",
    "apexA": [
      "162.159.140.98",
      "172.66.0.96"
    ],
    "apexAaaa": [
      "2606:4700:7::60",
      "2a06:98c1:58::60"
    ],
    "wwwCname": "walrus-app-kzog6.ondigitalocean.app",
    "note": "The zone is clean: the four Google A records and the four Google AAAA records are gone, replaced by DigitalOcean's two A and two AAAA values. The clean-vantage resolver still returned one stale Google AAAA (2001:4860:4802:38::15) alongside the two DigitalOcean ones -- residual cache inside the 600s TTL, expected to decay on its own and not a zone defect.",
    "untouched": "NS, the five MX records and the four TXT records were verified still present and unmodified; the AAAA failure mode the earlier guidance flagged (leaving IPv6 clients on Google while IPv4 moved) did not occur."
  },
